AB  - Data selection plays a crucial role in optimizing language model training. For automatically generated instruction datasets, the quality of evaluation becomes even more critical. We propose an automatic hybrid data selection method for instruction datasets that combines two approaches: the data-centric Organized-Action-Knowledge (OAK) Tree and the model-centric variability score method. Our experimental results demonstrate that our proposed method achieves comparable performance across 6 benchmark datasets while using only half of the training data compared to the full self-instruction dataset. Notably, this approach showed a 4.40% improvement in performance compared to using the entire dataset.
