KW  - On-policy distillation
KW  - Large language models
KW  - Model compression
KW  - Policy optimization
KW  - Knowledge distillation
AB  - The unprecedented scaling of Large Language Models (LLMs) has led to prohibitive computational costs in both training and deployment, intensifying the imperative for efficient model compression. Knowledge Distillation (KD), which transfers capability from resource-intensive teachers to compact students, has emerged as a leading paradigm. However, conventional off-policy KD suffers from exposure bias, as the training sequences are sampled from the teacher’s distribution, inducing a train-test mismatch. On-Policy Distillation (OPD), which grounds the distillation objective on trajectories sampled from a student-dependent behavioral policy and leverages teacher feedback on those trajectories, stands as a compelling alternative to mitigate these deficiencies. Nevertheless, the rapidly expanding OPD literature still lacks a systematic survey. In this survey, we organize OPD methods along a fundamental structural axis: teacher logit accessibility, yielding a dichotomy between white-box and black-box approaches. We review white-box OPD, encompassing vanilla OPD, self-distillation, and multi-teacher distillation. We summarize black-box OPD, an underexplored yet important direction, given that frontier teachers are increasingly available only through black-box application programming interfaces (APIs). To foster a comprehensive understanding of OPD, we analyze its modeling differences across two orthogonal dimensions: token-level versus sequence-level supervision granularity, and Generalized Knowledge Distillation (GKD)-Style versus Policy Gradient (PG)-Style optimization. Finally, we characterize prevalent failure modes in OPD, summarize the corresponding recovery strategies, and distill these findings into a practical decision flowchart for method selection. By integrating algorithmic innovations, theoretical insights, and industrial practices, this survey provides a comprehensive overview for researchers and practitioners to understand, diagnose, and advance the frontiers of OPD.
