AB  - In automated postal and logistics operations, Visual Parcel Invoice Understanding technology (VPIU) addresses the challenging task of recognizing named entities such as addresses, names, and phone numbers. In particular, the VPIU performance is significantly reduced when the addresses are extracted. Therefore, we propose a novel Retrieval-augmented-VPIU model (Re-VPIU). The proposed Re-VPIU consists of a Document Understanding Transformer (DONUT) for information extraction and a Large Language Model (LLM) with Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for information correction. First, using an end-to-end approach, the DONUT extracts information regarding addresses, names, and phone numbers from the invoice images. Next, the RAG detects and corrects errors in the extracted address information according to the Korean address database and prompts. Proposed Re-VPIU model is the first application of RAG in the context of visual document understanding. Unlike traditional models, Re-VPIU does not require retraining to incorporate new address data, as it dynamically integrates external knowledge through retrieval. Furthermore, it enables both character- and word-level corrections simultaneously, leveraging the linguistic capabilities of LLMs. To validate the proposed method's effectiveness, several comparative experiments were conducted using a Korean invoice dataset. The experiments showed that the proposed method achieved an F1 Score of 83.42 % when evaluating the accuracy of the complete extraction, which was 12.17 % higher than that of the current state-of-the-art model.
