AB  - In industrial environments where safety and compliance are critical, accessing accurate and context-specific information in real time is essential. This paper presents a lightweight framework that integrates Generative AI with a domain-specific ontology to support Health, Safety, and Environment (HSE) knowledge management. The system combines a Large Language Model (LLM) with a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline, using SPARQL queries and structured knowledge to produce grounded, context-aware responses to technical and regulatory questions. Results from initial evaluations demonstrate the framework’s ability to improve accuracy and relevance in answering real-world HSE queries, while avoiding the need for fine-tuning. The proposed architecture offers a scalable, low-maintenance solution that aligns with Industry 5.0 principles and has potential for broader deployment across safety-critical domains.
